# To enable agent verification of manual facts, uncomment and edit:
# - label: facts configuration
#   id: .config
#   agent: claude
#   batch-size: 10
# Or run: facts config set agent claude

# domain
- a Dot is a white light launched from one end of the strip and moving toward the opposite end @spec
- the Scoring Zone is a contiguous pulsing-yellow target region on the LED strip @spec
- Progress is represented by successful collisions shrinking the Scoring Zone toward its configured minimum and increasing its pulse frequency, not by a numeric score @spec

# gameplay

## input-and-motion
- pressing or holding either endpoint button launches a Dot from that end whenever that side has no active Dot @spec
- a launched Dot remains white while moving and deactivates after leaving the opposite end @spec

## collisions
- two active Dots collide when their opposing paths meet or cross @spec
- a collision succeeds when at least one pixel occupied or crossed by the Dots during the collision step lies inside the Scoring Zone @spec
- a successful collision runs a whole-strip green animation and then removes both Dots @spec
- a missed collision displays a three-pixel red marker centered on the collision for seven render frames and removes both Dots @spec

## progression
- a successful collision clears consecutive misses, reduces the Scoring Zone toward its configured minimum size, increases its pulse frequency, and randomly relocates it @spec
- a missed collision increments the consecutive-miss count @spec
- the third consecutive miss flashes the entire strip red, restores the Scoring Zone's configured initial size and pulse speed, randomly relocates it, and clears the miss count @spec

## scoring-zone
- the configured Scoring Zone size equals the number of yellow pixels it occupies @spec
